TurtleGit for Mac is an independent, unofficial port project.
Upstream TortoiseGit: https://github.com/TortoiseGit/TortoiseGit
Official upstream project: https://tortoisegit.org/
Upstream source and license are copyright their respective contributors.
The LICENSE file is retained from upstream TortoiseGit (GPL version 2).
No affiliation or endorsement by the upstream project is claimed.
New Swift implementation in this repository is licensed under GPL version 2.
The upstream audit baseline is documented in docs/upstream.json.
Apple frameworks and separately installed Git retain their own licenses.

Command and status icon artwork is copied unchanged from TortoiseGit resources.
Those icons were derived from the TortoiseSVN project: https://tortoisesvn.net/
The upstream notice also names https://tortoisesvn.tigris.org/ (historical site).
We use the GNU GPL alternative offered by the upstream resource license.
The original resource license, source paths and SHA-256 hashes are retained in
Sources/TurtleGitCore/Resources/Icons/ and bundled with the shared framework.
Copyright (c) 2006-2007 The TortoiseSVN Project. All rights reserved.

AppStore preparation bundles a pinned Git engine built from its unmodified
upstream source archive (https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/). Git is
licensed under GPL v2. Its corresponding source archive, COPYING, retained
third-party notices and reconstruction scripts are included under
Contents/Helpers/Git/share/licenses/git/. Configuration/GitRuntime.json records
the version, source URL and checksum. macOS system libraries are not redistributed.

The app bundles EditorConfig C Core and statically linked PCRE2. Their original
license texts, pinned source/test archives and reconstruction script are retained
under Contents/Helpers/EditorConfig/. Configuration/EditorConfigRuntime.json
records source versions and checksums. EditorConfig includes Simplified/New/
Revised BSD and per-file notices; PCRE2 retains its BSD license and exceptions.
Consult the included license texts and complete corresponding sources.

The issue-matching helper adapts the std::wregex matching algorithm from
TortoiseGit src/TortoiseProc/ProjectProperties.cpp, copyright (C) 2003-2021,
2023-2025 TortoiseGit, under GPL version 2 or later. Its UTF-16 process transport
is implemented for macOS. Corresponding source, reconstruction and validation
scripts, and the GPL license are bundled under Contents/Helpers/IssueRegex/.
See docs/ISSUE-TRACKER-PARITY.md for the pinned upstream audit and limitations.
Its UTF-8 message styling adapts Utils/MiscUI/SciEdit.cpp::MarkEnteredBugID,
copyright (C) 2009-2026 TortoiseGit and (C) 2003-2008, 2012-2020, 2025
TortoiseSVN, also under GPL version 2 or later. These notices are retained
in the helper's bundled corresponding source.
Sources/TurtleGitCore/IssueTracker.swift adapts the same project's configuration,
issue-template, validation, URL-escaping and sign-off behavior, retaining its
copyright attribution and GPL version 2 or later notice.
Sources/TurtleGitCore/MessageURLFinder.swift adapts URLFinder.h's URL/email
scanning algorithm, copyright (C) 2009-2023 TortoiseGit and (C) 2003-2008,
2013, 2018, 2020 TortoiseSVN, under GPL version 2 or later. The native scheme
gate and UTF-16 scalar traversal are described in the issue-tracker audit.
Sources/TurtleGitCore/MessageFormatting.swift adapts SciEdit.cpp's marker
formatting, retaining the TortoiseGit/TortoiseSVN notices above and GPL version
2 or later attribution. Marker text remains unchanged in committed messages.

Sources/TurtleGitCore/MessageCompletion.swift adapts CommitDlg.cpp filename
catalog generation and SciEdit.cpp completion matching under GPL version 2 or
later, retaining their TortoiseGit/TortoiseSVN copyright notices. The native
popup reuses the upstream file.ico unchanged; its provenance is recorded in
Sources/TurtleGitCore/Resources/Icons/provenance.json.

Sources/TurtleGitCore/MessageSnippets.swift adapts CommitDlg.cpp snippet parsing
and selection expansion, under GPL version 2 or later with its TortoiseGit
copyright notice. The original shipped snippet.txt and snippet.ico are retained
unchanged, with pinned source and SHA-256 provenance in their resource folders.

The helper also adapts CommitDlg.cpp::ScanFile capture-group extraction under
GPL version 2 or later. MessageCodeSymbols.swift adapts its definition parsing
and capture transport, retaining TortoiseGit attribution. The original
autolist.txt is bundled unchanged with pinned provenance. File scanning and
complete native code-completion integration remain under development.

MessageCodeText.swift adapts TortoiseGitMerge FileTextLines.cpp encoding detection
and decode-filter units, under GPL version 2 or later. Copyright (C) 2016, 2019,
2021, 2023, 2025 TortoiseGit and (C) 2007-2016, 2019 TortoiseSVN. Windows ACP and
malformed UTF-8 decoding require documented native adaptations.

MessageCodeScanner.swift adapts CommitDlg.cpp changed-file traversal, catalog
insertion order, regex caching, timeout and size gates under GPL version 2 or
later, retaining its TortoiseGit notice. Raw decoded UTF-16 units are passed
unchanged through the existing helper transport. The native Commit popup consumes this catalog with the original code.ico
artwork. Complete editor parity and signed sandbox acceptance remain under
development.

RepositoryBrowser.swift and the native RepositoryBrowserWindow.swift adapt
TortoiseGit RepositoryBrowser.cpp tree/list/revision workflows under GPL version
2 or later. Copyright (C) 2009-2026 TortoiseGit and (C) 2003-2013 TortoiseSVN.
Original menurepobrowse.ico and executable/symlink/external overlay artwork are
retained unchanged with pinned provenance. Complete browser context commands,
drag export and signed sandbox acceptance remain under development.

Repository Browser historical drag export adapts RepositoryBrowser.cpp recursive
selection and GitDataObject.cpp/.h file-content/descriptors under GPL version 2
or later. Copyright (C) 2016-2019, 2021-2023, 2025 TortoiseGit and (C) 2007-2014
TortoiseSVN. Native table-row item providers replace Windows OLE for this consumer;
other GitDataObject consumers, Finder drop acceptance and signed transfer remain
under development. Symlink blobs export as regular target text; gitlinks are
skipped. Native export copies preserve executable permission as a macOS adaptation.

FormatPatch.swift adapts the command construction in FormatPatchCommand.cpp
and the sole-for-merge FETCH_HEAD choice in Git.cpp, under GPL version 2 or later.
Copyright (C) 2009, 2015-2016, 2018-2019, 2023, 2026 TortoiseGit and (C) 2007-2008
TortoiseSVN (FormatPatchCommand); Copyright (C) 2008-2026 TortoiseGit (Git.cpp).
FormatPatchWindow.swift adapts FormatPatchDlg.cpp/.h and IDD_FORMAT_PATCH under
GPL version 2 or later. Copyright (C) 2008-2014, 2016-2017, 2019-2020, 2023-2025
TortoiseGit. AppKit history fields and radio buttons replace MFC controls, and
native mail composition replaces the Windows Send Mail handoff. Complete mail,
progress cancellation and signed sandbox verification remain pending.

Format Patch Log presets adapt GitLogListAction.cpp ID_CREATE_PATCH and
GitLogListBase.cpp selection eligibility, under GPL version 2 or later.
Copyright (C) 2008-2026 TortoiseGit and (C) 2005-2007 Marco Costalba.
Original menupatch.ico is retained unchanged for the Log context command.

Native Format Patch cancellation follows ProgressDlg.cpp's interrupt then stop
child-process workflow under GPL version 2 or later. Copyright (C) 2008-2020,
2022-2026 TortoiseGit. CancellableGitProcess.swift uses a
macOS POSIX spawn process group instead of Windows process-tree enumeration.

UnifiedDiffViewer.swift and UnifiedDiffViewerSettings.swift adapt the separate
GNU patch viewer preference and Shift inversion from AppUtils.cpp and
SettingsProgsDiff.cpp under GPL version 2 or later. AppUtils: Copyright (C)
2008-2026 TortoiseGit and (C) 2003-2011, 2013-2014 TortoiseSVN. SettingsProgsDiff:
Copyright (C) 2008-2011, 2013-2016 TortoiseGit and (C) 2003-2007, 2011 TortoiseSVN.
macOS application bundles, document opening and security bookmarks replace the
Windows viewer command for this partial replacement; command templates remain
pending. External viewers receive an exact read-only temporary byte copy.
